{#
  Generates a Markdown twin of each HTML reference page, so an agent consuming
  this design system gets the component markup without fetching a ~36KB page
  that is ~91% chrome.

  Each top-level <section> becomes a heading plus a fenced HTML block holding
  that section's rendered markup. Generated from `templateContent`, so it is
  the final markup (includes expanded, `url` filter applied) and cannot drift
  from the page it documents.

  Caveat, stated in the output as well: these pages lay out each demo beside
  its description, so the fenced markup contains that documentation
  scaffolding (`.row` / `.col-*` wrappers) alongside the component itself.

  `| safe` throughout: the output is Markdown, so Nunjucks HTML autoescaping
  would turn every fenced example into unusable `&lt;p&gt;` entities.
-#}
{%- set sections = doc.templateContent | referenceSections -%}
